      "math_academy_id": "q-129527",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=36$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=4.$ Find $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X-\\frac{1}{2}Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X-\\frac{1}{2}Y]={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 36+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 4=5.\n$$",
